The autoUpdate orientation note is kept deliberately even though it was
initially waved off: the skill is general-purpose and must behave the
same regardless of the user's rerere.autoUpdate setting, so the
robustness note earns its place on its own merits, not because of any
one machine's config.

The worktree-safety fix (rev-parse over a literal .git/MERGE_HEAD path)
is opportunistic — it hasn't bitten us, but the rev-parse form is
strictly more correct and costs nothing.
